00:17:09,762 --> 00:17:12,390
Just relax and think
that you're walking toward me. Okay?

260
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:14,601
You got this.

261
00:17:15,518 --> 00:17:16,728
- Okay.
- Take two.

262
00:17:16,811 --> 00:17:18,855
- Let's roll again.
- Let's roll again.

263
00:17:20,273 --> 00:17:21,399
Now, slate it.

264
00:17:21,983 --> 00:17:23,485
- And...
- Wait.

265
00:17:26,488 --> 00:17:27,489
Cue.

266
00:17:37,707 --> 00:17:40,210
I'm sorry. You are...

267
00:17:44,631 --> 00:17:45,840
the one I was looking for.

268
00:18:03,024 --> 00:18:04,108
Cut!

269
00:18:04,275 --> 00:18:07,320
What's wrong, Chan?
You got the line wrong.

270
00:18:07,403 --> 00:18:10,448
Goodness. I'm sorry.
Let me do that again. I'm sorry.

271
00:18:12,325 --> 00:18:13,618
Let's do another take.

272
00:18:26,714 --> 00:18:28,883
- Oh, wow.
- Right here.

273
00:18:31,928 --> 00:18:34,097
Seo-jun, are you putting
stickers on his face?

274
00:18:35,431 --> 00:18:37,267
Great job.
Keep doing that for me. Thanks.

275
00:18:38,893 --> 00:18:40,520
Put some more on him.

276
00:18:43,690 --> 00:18:45,817
This is great. I'm so happy.

277
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:48,111
I'm even happier to see Ha-gi
for the first time in ages.

278
00:18:48,194 --> 00:18:49,779
I'm sorry to bother you
on your day off.

279
00:18:49,862 --> 00:18:52,448
But my kids were begging to see you

280
00:18:52,532 --> 00:18:54,242
and asked me to drag you here.

281
00:18:55,159 --> 00:18:57,829
Seo-jun and Seo-yeon,
stop bothering him now.

282
00:18:57,912 --> 00:18:59,664
You'll make
my life at work difficult.

283
00:19:00,081 --> 00:19:02,500
- Go over there and play.
- Yes, go there and run around.

284
00:19:02,917 --> 00:19:04,085
Yes, you can run all you want.

285
00:19:06,629 --> 00:19:08,047
It's okay, Seong-wook.

286
00:19:09,132 --> 00:19:11,634
It's nice to get out for a change.

287
00:19:12,260 --> 00:19:14,971
And it's nice to see
Mrs. Chae after so long.

288
00:19:15,054 --> 00:19:16,806
Gosh, that brings me back
to the old days.

289
00:19:16,889 --> 00:19:18,308
When you just started working

290
00:19:18,391 --> 00:19:22,228
you'd chase me around like a chick,
calling me, "Ms. Chae."

291
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:25,398
And you went around
calling me, "Mr. CEO."

292
00:19:25,481 --> 00:19:27,483
If only my business hadn't failed.

293
00:19:27,567 --> 00:19:30,486
Respect him at work
and watch what you say.

294
00:19:30,570 --> 00:19:33,573
We have a mountain of debt
because of that ruined business.

295
00:19:34,032 --> 00:19:37,535
Please show my husband your favor,
CEO Kang Ha-gi.

296
00:19:37,619 --> 00:19:39,203
- A raise, please.
- Don't mention it.

297
00:19:39,787 --> 00:19:41,873
I'm so grateful for his help.

298
00:19:42,749 --> 00:19:45,084
I should've planned
this get-together sooner.

299
00:19:45,627 --> 00:19:47,337
Come over to my place.

300
00:19:47,420 --> 00:19:48,796
I'll treat you to dinner.

301
00:19:49,547 --> 00:19:52,925
Really?
I'd love to eat at your place.

302
00:19:53,009 --> 00:19:54,552
Stop. What do you mean?

303
00:19:54,802 --> 00:19:56,429
Why? What did I say just now?

304
00:19:56,512 --> 00:19:57,847
- You'd love to eat there?
- No.

305
00:19:57,930 --> 00:19:59,724
I think the kids are fighting.

306
00:20:04,062 --> 00:20:05,104
Is this it?

307
00:20:12,987 --> 00:20:14,197
I can't see anything.

308
00:20:24,624 --> 00:20:25,958
- You found it all right.
- Yes.

309
00:20:26,542 --> 00:20:27,752
- Get in.
- Okay.

310
00:20:36,427 --> 00:20:38,346
- Shall we?
- Okay.

311
00:20:38,429 --> 00:20:41,724
Just drop me at any subway station
on your way.

312
00:20:42,266 --> 00:20:43,309
What do you mean?

313
00:20:44,102 --> 00:20:45,645
- You have to grant me a wish.
- What?

314
00:20:46,437 --> 00:20:47,438
But back there...

315
00:20:49,273 --> 00:20:50,316
Did you think

316
00:20:50,900 --> 00:20:53,277
my wish was
for you to show up at my shoot?

317
00:20:56,989 --> 00:20:59,826
I wanted to get some good food
with you after the shoot.

318
00:21:00,785 --> 00:21:02,995
But the shoot ran long

319
00:21:03,079 --> 00:21:05,206
and I had to cancel my reservation.

320
00:21:08,126 --> 00:21:10,044
Come to my place. I'll cook for you.

321
00:21:13,798 --> 00:21:14,799
Pardon?

322
00:21:17,218 --> 00:21:19,595
Your place?

323
00:21:20,179 --> 00:21:21,180
Yes.

324
00:21:21,556 --> 00:21:22,849
You mean

325
00:21:23,391 --> 00:21:24,809
I'm going to your place?

326
00:21:25,351 --> 00:21:26,936
Yes, it's right around the corner.

327
00:21:28,229 --> 00:21:31,023
<i>What's going on? Am I dreaming?</i>

328
00:21:32,150 --> 00:21:33,443
<i>My heart is about to burst.</i>

329
00:21:33,943 --> 00:21:35,403
- Buckle up.
- What? Okay.

330
00:21:41,868 --> 00:21:44,203
<i>Tech neck, rounded shoulders,
and a herniated disc too.</i>

331
00:21:44,287 --> 00:21:45,663
<i>You're a whole mess.</i>

332
00:21:45,788 --> 00:21:48,332
<i>You should pick up
a workout like Pilates.</i>

333
00:21:48,583 --> 00:21:50,835
Why would a guy do Pilates?

334
00:21:50,918 --> 00:21:53,129
Without this curve,
my neck would be stiff.

335
00:21:53,212 --> 00:21:55,548
My shoulders are obviously straight,
and so is my back.

336
00:21:57,383 --> 00:21:58,468
I'm totally fine.

337
00:21:59,719 --> 00:22:01,637
SMOOTH

338
00:22:10,313 --> 00:22:12,356
{\an8}APPARATUS PILATES
POSTURE CORRECTION

339
00:22:14,233 --> 00:22:15,401
Smooth?

340
00:22:15,485 --> 00:22:16,819
HYBRID PILATES

341
00:22:18,362 --> 00:22:19,405
The doctor was right.

342
00:22:20,698 --> 00:22:23,326
My neck hurts. It does.

343
00:22:38,883 --> 00:22:40,426
This is amazing.

344
00:22:58,986 --> 00:23:01,197
- This way.
- Okay.

345
00:23:02,907 --> 00:23:05,660
<i>Walking into his place together</i>

346
00:23:06,077 --> 00:23:07,703
<i>makes us feel like a couple...</i>

347
00:23:08,287 --> 00:23:09,664
<i>Get a grip on yourself, Da-reum.</i>

348
00:23:10,122 --> 00:23:13,334
<i>He only invited me home
because he can't eat outside freely.</i>

349
00:23:13,417 --> 00:23:15,336
<i>Cut it out with your filthy delusion.</i>

350
00:23:21,374 --> 00:23:22,542
What should I make?

351
00:23:24,461 --> 00:23:26,045
CREAM RISOTTO

352
00:23:27,630 --> 00:23:29,466
{\an8}2022 GOLDEN CREST AWARD
BEST ACTOR LEE CHAN

353
00:23:29,549 --> 00:23:30,675
{\an8}Yes, I remember.

354
00:23:40,101 --> 00:23:42,520
{\an8}That was the Rookie Award he won
after he had just started acting.

355
00:23:44,397 --> 00:23:46,399
I cried a river back then.

356
00:23:49,986 --> 00:23:51,321
- Da-reum.
- Yes?

357
00:23:51,404 --> 00:23:52,781
You can go upstairs and take a tour.

358
00:23:53,907 --> 00:23:55,700
May I do that?

359
00:23:55,784 --> 00:23:56,868
Of course.

360
00:23:57,118 --> 00:23:58,328
I'll call you when I'm done.

361
00:23:59,370 --> 00:24:00,413
Okay.

362
00:24:01,790 --> 00:24:03,291
- Feel free to relax.
- Okay.

363
00:24:08,338 --> 00:24:09,380
What the heck.

364
00:24:10,048 --> 00:24:11,174
CREAM GNOCCHI

365
00:24:15,720 --> 00:24:17,847
Please excuse me.

366
00:24:25,355 --> 00:24:26,356
My gosh.

367
00:24:27,273 --> 00:24:29,776
This was the shoot
he did with Photographer Yeong-su.

368
00:24:30,109 --> 00:24:31,778
This wasn't in the pictorial.

369
00:24:32,362 --> 00:24:35,698
Am I really allowed to see
these unreleased photos?

370
00:24:38,159 --> 00:24:40,662
Look at his eyes. Insane.

371
00:24:45,083 --> 00:24:48,044
So this is where
he streams live from time to time.

372
00:24:48,503 --> 00:24:50,171
It's so cool.

373
00:24:54,843 --> 00:24:56,219
He's so great.

374
00:25:06,813 --> 00:25:09,232
Does he still make music?

375
00:25:09,691 --> 00:25:11,943
Da-reum, dinner's ready.
Come on down.

376
00:25:12,026 --> 00:25:13,027
Okay.

377
00:25:20,577 --> 00:25:22,078
{\an8}CREAM GNOCCHI, FISH ROE PASTA

378
00:25:28,877 --> 00:25:31,880
Did you make all these?

379
00:25:33,548 --> 00:25:34,841
You're amazing.

380
00:25:35,049 --> 00:25:37,468
- You're teasing me.
- I'm not.

381
00:25:38,887 --> 00:25:40,179
It's fine as long as it's good.

382
00:25:40,889 --> 00:25:43,933
I tried doing my best,
but I don't know how good it is.

383
00:25:46,352 --> 00:25:47,353
Thank you.

384
00:25:54,110 --> 00:25:55,528
It's really good.

385
00:25:56,821 --> 00:25:58,364
It's like a dish
made by a famous chef.

386
00:25:58,448 --> 00:26:00,867
Really? I did get some help.

387
00:26:01,659 --> 00:26:03,745
Eat up, Da-reum. Here.

388
00:26:04,329 --> 00:26:05,455
Thank you.

389
00:26:12,378 --> 00:26:15,214
<i>I'm too nervous
to enjoy this right now.</i>

390
00:26:16,049 --> 00:26:17,759
I hope you weren't lying
when you said it was good.

391
00:26:20,970 --> 00:26:23,932
I'm just a bit nervous.

392
00:26:24,891 --> 00:26:27,852
- If it's too much, just leave it.
- No, it's not.

393
00:26:28,269 --> 00:26:31,022
<i>Usually, I would've finished
all of these in three minutes.</i>

394
00:26:34,359 --> 00:26:35,401
One second.

395
00:26:47,580 --> 00:26:49,791
YOON CHO-YI

396
00:26:59,759 --> 00:27:01,177
How's work?

397
00:27:04,555 --> 00:27:06,099
It's probably not easy
to work with Ha-gi.

398
00:27:09,560 --> 00:27:10,853
It's not.

399
00:27:11,479 --> 00:27:13,064
When he comes next to me

400
00:27:13,606 --> 00:27:15,566
I get chills down my spine.

401
00:27:17,110 --> 00:27:19,237
He's someone
I can't seem to get close to.

402
00:27:19,737 --> 00:27:20,863
He's like that.

403
00:27:21,030 --> 00:27:23,992
He never lets his guard down
around people.

404
00:27:24,075 --> 00:27:26,327
Yes, exactly.

405
00:27:26,661 --> 00:27:30,498
His office is impeccably neat
right down to every single pen.

406
00:27:30,957 --> 00:27:32,875
He's probably like that at home too.

407
00:27:33,376 --> 00:27:34,419
Right?

408
00:27:43,177 --> 00:27:44,721
Hey, this is really good.

409
00:27:45,263 --> 00:27:46,389
Eat up.

410
00:27:47,390 --> 00:27:48,975
- Go.
- Let's go.

411
00:27:49,767 --> 00:27:52,061
- Guys, no running.
- Don't you love his place?

412
00:27:52,145 --> 00:27:53,479
This isn't our place!

413
00:27:53,563 --> 00:27:54,814
- I wish it were.
- Hey.

414
00:27:54,897 --> 00:27:56,691
<i>The one thing Ha-gi can't stand</i>

415
00:27:57,191 --> 00:27:59,027
<i>is anything
that's hectic and disorderly.</i>

416
00:27:59,444 --> 00:28:01,320
<i>He rarely ever invites people over.</i>

417
00:28:01,571 --> 00:28:02,864
Sorry, Ha-gi.

418
00:28:03,614 --> 00:28:05,533
- It's okay.
- Stop running!

419
00:28:06,784 --> 00:28:07,869
What's this?

420
00:28:09,120 --> 00:28:11,164
<i>- But one funny thing about him.</i>
- Hey! No!

421
00:28:13,916 --> 00:28:15,418
- Uncle Ha-gi...
- Uncle Ha-gi...

422
00:28:21,174 --> 00:28:22,216
Fine.

423
00:28:23,468 --> 00:28:24,886
Go ahead.

424
00:28:31,267 --> 00:28:33,853
<i>He has the weakest spot
for people within his boundary.</i>

425
00:28:36,522 --> 00:28:38,733
He was really nosy when we were kids.

426
00:28:39,192 --> 00:28:40,318
You mean, Mr. Kang?

427
00:28:41,069 --> 00:28:42,278
That's hard to imagine.

428
00:28:44,197 --> 00:28:47,116
The reason we got close
was thanks to his nosiness.

429
00:28:48,284 --> 00:28:50,453
I wasn't looking to make friends

430
00:28:50,828 --> 00:28:51,954
but Ha-gi

431
00:28:52,747 --> 00:28:54,248
kept pestering me.

432
00:28:56,125 --> 00:28:57,794
<i>I transferred
when I was in 10th grade</i>

433
00:28:58,503 --> 00:28:59,879
<i>and had trouble adapting.</i>

434
00:29:00,838 --> 00:29:01,839
<i>I got bullied too.</i>

435
00:29:03,800 --> 00:29:05,760
- There you are, my friend.
- What?

436
00:29:06,677 --> 00:29:07,678
What are you doing?

437
00:29:07,762 --> 00:29:09,013
Time to pay
this week's friendship fee.

438
00:29:09,263 --> 00:29:10,348
Cut it out.

439
00:29:12,558 --> 00:29:13,559
Thanks a lot.

440
00:29:17,021 --> 00:29:18,189
Oh, sorry.

441
00:29:18,397 --> 00:29:20,024
He's a player on my team.

442
00:29:20,233 --> 00:29:21,859
Do you have business with him?

443
00:29:23,152 --> 00:29:24,654
Darn it.

444
00:29:24,737 --> 00:29:27,281
<i>Ha-gi was the school president,
who got good grades</i>

445
00:29:27,365 --> 00:29:29,408
<i>and was good at basketball.
The typical golden boy.</i>

446
00:29:29,492 --> 00:29:30,493
Let's go.

447
00:29:32,245 --> 00:29:33,412
I'll get you later.

448
00:29:41,921 --> 00:29:42,922
Hey.

449
00:29:44,257 --> 00:29:46,175
We really need
more players on our team.

450
00:29:46,884 --> 00:29:48,052
Can you play one game with us?

451
00:29:48,970 --> 00:29:49,971
What?

452
00:29:51,097 --> 00:29:53,057
- Come on.
- Let's split into teams.

453
00:29:53,141 --> 00:29:54,475
- Okay.
- Come on.

454
00:29:54,559 --> 00:29:56,644
The losers treat the winners
to snacks at the snack bar.

455
00:29:56,978 --> 00:29:58,813
- Let's go.
- Come on.

456
00:30:09,198 --> 00:30:10,241
Hey, Chan.

457
00:30:10,825 --> 00:30:11,826
Time for a snack bar run.

458
00:30:16,581 --> 00:30:17,582
Hey.

459
00:30:18,374 --> 00:30:19,750
What are you waiting for? Let's go.

460
00:30:20,710 --> 00:30:21,752
What?

461
00:30:22,295 --> 00:30:25,381
- Come on.
<i>- And he was a warm-hearted kid</i>

462
00:30:25,631 --> 00:30:27,508
<i>who couldn't see anyone get left out.</i>

463
00:30:32,305 --> 00:30:33,806
- Go, Ha-gi.
- Go, Ha-gi.

464
00:30:34,098 --> 00:30:36,309
Over here!

465
00:30:36,392 --> 00:30:39,061
- Nice job!
- Oh, no.

466
00:30:40,396 --> 00:30:41,772
You got this, Ha-gi.

467
00:30:41,856 --> 00:30:43,274
Just do your thing. Yes.

468
00:30:43,524 --> 00:30:44,775
Yes, that's it.

469
00:30:45,151 --> 00:30:47,195
- Nice job!
- Okay!

470
00:30:47,820 --> 00:30:49,113
Great job!

471
00:30:51,782 --> 00:30:53,075
Nice job!

472
00:30:53,159 --> 00:30:55,036
That was awesome, Ha-gi!

473
00:30:55,119 --> 00:30:56,829
- Awesome job.
- Let's go.

474
00:30:59,290 --> 00:31:01,834
<i>Thanks to him,
I gradually changed too.</i>

475
00:31:03,002 --> 00:31:05,588
- Hey, wait.
- Let's go!

476
00:31:06,088 --> 00:31:07,298
What do you want to eat?

477
00:31:07,715 --> 00:31:08,925
What do you feel like?

478
00:31:09,008 --> 00:31:10,426
<i>It was a lot of fun</i>

479
00:31:10,635 --> 00:31:13,095
<i>- to spend time with Ha-gi.</i>
- I don't know. What should we eat?

480
00:31:13,846 --> 00:31:16,140
<i>I even stuck around at his place
and had dinner every day.</i>

481
00:31:16,224 --> 00:31:17,308
It smells great.

482
00:31:17,558 --> 00:31:19,936
<i>- My parents always came home late.</i>
- Thank you.

483
00:31:20,019 --> 00:31:21,354
Thank you.

484
00:31:21,729 --> 00:31:22,897
Hey, you made bulgogi.

485
00:31:22,980 --> 00:31:24,690
Yes, because it's your favorite.

486
00:31:39,705 --> 00:31:40,706
Eat up.

487
00:31:48,297 --> 00:31:49,757
Just as you helped me

488
00:31:51,050 --> 00:31:52,927
overcome my darkest times

489
00:31:54,553 --> 00:31:56,764
you had Mr. Kang with you.

490
00:31:58,516 --> 00:31:59,642
He is

491
00:32:00,434 --> 00:32:02,520
my one and only friend.

492
00:32:04,939 --> 00:32:07,316
Maybe everyone wanted
to be friends with you

493
00:32:07,400 --> 00:32:09,527
but you just didn't realize it?

494
00:32:10,111 --> 00:32:12,154
No way. I wasn't that popular.

495
00:32:13,322 --> 00:32:15,032
- You're lying.
- I'm serious.

496
00:32:15,533 --> 00:32:17,118
Ha-gi was much more popular.

497
00:32:17,660 --> 00:32:18,661
Really?

498
00:32:20,037 --> 00:32:21,872
I guess it shows

499
00:32:23,749 --> 00:32:25,876
whether a person
has always been loved

500
00:32:29,380 --> 00:32:30,589
or they haven't.

501
00:32:38,222 --> 00:32:40,057
Everyone leaves me in the end.

502
00:32:42,435 --> 00:32:43,561
I wouldn't.

503
00:32:44,562 --> 00:32:46,314
For the last ten years... No.

504
00:32:46,981 --> 00:32:48,024
To be exact

505
00:32:48,899 --> 00:32:51,319
I've liked only you
for the last 11 years and ten months.

506
00:32:51,402 --> 00:32:53,821
I have never set my eyes
on anyone else, not even once.

507
00:32:53,904 --> 00:32:56,574
And I will continue to like only you.

508
00:33:01,120 --> 00:33:04,123
<i>Wait, what have I done just now?</i>

509
00:33:04,832 --> 00:33:07,918
<i>Look how overwhelmed he is.</i>

510
00:33:08,919 --> 00:33:10,046
I mean

511
00:33:11,130 --> 00:33:12,173
as a fan.

512
00:33:12,256 --> 00:33:13,716
Completely as a fan.

513
00:33:14,216 --> 00:33:16,344
Just as a fan.

514
00:33:30,149 --> 00:33:31,275
Thanks for liking me.

515
00:33:33,152 --> 00:33:34,487
I'm not even a big deal

516
00:33:35,571 --> 00:33:37,907
but thank you for your support
over such a long time.

517
00:33:38,282 --> 00:33:39,367
Thank you.

518
00:33:39,742 --> 00:33:41,369
I want to thank you too.

519
00:33:43,412 --> 00:33:47,416
And I never thought
I'd see a day like this in my life.

520
00:33:49,502 --> 00:33:50,503
Da-reum.

521
00:33:50,920 --> 00:33:52,129
Can I ask you for a favor?

522
00:34:16,487 --> 00:34:17,696
What do you think about this song?

523
00:34:19,573 --> 00:34:20,866
I love it.

524
00:34:21,867 --> 00:34:25,371
It reminds me of old D.N.X songs.

525
00:34:27,998 --> 00:34:29,250
D.N.X.

526
00:34:30,835 --> 00:34:33,421
I only meant how the song sounded.

527
00:34:35,339 --> 00:34:36,424
I'm sorry.

528
00:34:36,590 --> 00:34:38,050
I shouldn't have brought it up.

529
00:34:38,134 --> 00:34:39,468
No, don't say that.

530
00:34:40,761 --> 00:34:42,221
I'm so grateful

531
00:34:42,596 --> 00:34:44,557
that you still think about D.N.X.

532
00:34:49,353 --> 00:34:50,396
Da-reum.

533
00:34:52,398 --> 00:34:54,358
Do you also want us to reunite?

534
00:34:55,693 --> 00:34:56,944
Yes, of course.

535
00:34:57,319 --> 00:34:59,447
All D-Angels would feel the same.

536
00:35:01,782 --> 00:35:04,368
It's actually meant
to be a D.N.X fan song.

537
00:35:06,620 --> 00:35:08,456
If we ever reunite

538
00:35:08,998 --> 00:35:10,374
I want to sing it with everyone.

539
00:35:12,501 --> 00:35:13,544
Chan...

540
00:35:14,420 --> 00:35:16,005
I also did the mixing.
Would you like to listen to it?

541
00:35:16,088 --> 00:35:17,965
Oh, yes. I'd love to listen to it.

542
00:35:34,940 --> 00:35:36,025
<i>What's this?</i>

543
00:35:36,901 --> 00:35:38,027
<i>What is this vibe?</i>

544
00:35:44,783 --> 00:35:47,286
<i>You're so slow.
What do you think this means?</i>

545
00:35:47,495 --> 00:35:49,497
<i>It's obviously a date.</i>

546
00:35:49,705 --> 00:35:51,415
<i>A fan is a woman too.</i>

547
00:35:52,541 --> 00:35:53,751
<i>What do I do?</i>

548
00:36:09,183 --> 00:36:10,184
- Da-reum.
- Yes?

549
00:36:20,027 --> 00:36:21,403
What are you guys doing?

550
00:36:26,909 --> 00:36:28,035
What are you doing here?

551
00:36:28,786 --> 00:36:30,496
Am I in the wrong place?

552
00:36:33,332 --> 00:36:34,750
Is it you this time?

553
00:36:35,292 --> 00:36:36,752
How was the fan meet with him?

554
00:36:37,419 --> 00:36:38,963
Did you enjoy it
to your heart's content?

555
00:36:39,755 --> 00:36:41,757
- Pardon?
- Come out. Let's talk outside.

556
00:36:42,883 --> 00:36:43,884
Did I

557
00:36:44,468 --> 00:36:46,887
walk in
when you were expecting something?

558
00:36:46,971 --> 00:36:47,972
Hey, Yoon Cho-yi.

559
00:36:53,269 --> 00:36:55,646
Oh, no. I guess I was right.

560
00:36:57,815 --> 00:36:59,984
Did you really think
there was something going on?

561
00:37:04,029 --> 00:37:06,782
- She's cute.
- What are you saying? Get out.

562
00:37:07,491 --> 00:37:09,368
No, I'll leave.

563
00:37:14,123 --> 00:37:15,624
Thank you for everything today,
Director Lee.

564
00:37:15,833 --> 00:37:18,043
I'm sorry, but if you don't mind,
I'll get going first.

565
00:37:18,961 --> 00:37:20,004
Da-reum.

566
00:37:24,883 --> 00:37:25,926
Da-reum.

567
00:37:35,894 --> 00:37:36,895
Da-reum.

568
00:37:47,323 --> 00:37:49,366
Chan, I'm sorry.

569
00:37:49,742 --> 00:37:51,368
I was such a bother today.

570
00:37:51,994 --> 00:37:53,287
You should get inside.

571
00:37:53,370 --> 00:37:55,998
- Da-reum, that's not it...
- Chan.

572
00:37:56,582 --> 00:37:57,625
Can you

573
00:37:58,834 --> 00:38:00,961
just let me go?

574
00:38:02,254 --> 00:38:03,297
I feel

575
00:38:05,799 --> 00:38:07,593
mortified right now.

576
00:38:48,550 --> 00:38:50,678
Why did I dress up?

577
00:38:52,846 --> 00:38:54,098
This is humiliating.

578
00:39:21,166 --> 00:39:22,459
How did you get in?

579
00:39:24,837 --> 00:39:27,047
The passcode to your door is
still the same.

580
00:39:28,716 --> 00:39:30,634
You must've kept it
because you wanted me to come in.

581
00:39:33,637 --> 00:39:34,972
The person who was just here...

582
00:39:36,014 --> 00:39:38,600
I had her over for a meal
because she was a special fan.

583
00:39:40,102 --> 00:39:42,146
She's not someone
you can talk to like that.

584
00:39:42,396 --> 00:39:45,232
Have you ever had me over
for anything when we were dating?

585
00:39:45,774 --> 00:39:46,942
What does she mean to you?

586
00:39:47,025 --> 00:39:48,694
Why are you treating her
like she's special?

587
00:39:48,777 --> 00:39:52,072
She rooted for me for ten years,
but I've never done anything for her.

588
00:39:53,532 --> 00:39:54,533
Right.

589
00:39:54,783 --> 00:39:56,493
You have always been like that.

590
00:39:56,744 --> 00:39:59,288
You act like a good person
on the outside.

591
00:39:59,955 --> 00:40:02,499
You think you won't hurt other people
like you hurt me?

592
00:40:03,125 --> 00:40:04,877
Whoever you choose to date

593
00:40:05,544 --> 00:40:06,587
you'll still be the same.

594
00:40:11,467 --> 00:40:14,136
Ha-gi, thanks for everything today.
See you next time.

595
00:40:14,219 --> 00:40:15,512
- Bye.
- Say bye to Uncle Ha-gi.

596
00:40:15,596 --> 00:40:16,889
- Bye.
- Bye, Uncle Ha-gi.

597
00:40:16,972 --> 00:40:18,432
See you.

598
00:40:18,515 --> 00:40:20,476
- Bye.
- Take care.

599
00:40:20,559 --> 00:40:23,687
See you. Bye.

600
00:40:32,571 --> 00:40:34,281
A sticker remover.

601
00:40:36,158 --> 00:40:37,159
Where can I get it?

602
00:40:48,462 --> 00:40:50,589
BEAUTY TRIO GROUP CHAT

603
00:40:51,173 --> 00:40:54,051
<i>Namda! Are you still with Chan?</i>

604
00:40:54,134 --> 00:40:56,637
<i>Are you alive or not?
Why aren't you answering?</i>

605
00:41:05,771 --> 00:41:08,357
<i>BITTER SWEET</i>

606
00:41:10,275 --> 00:41:14,154
<i>I hope they aren't fighting
because of me.</i>

607
00:41:16,406 --> 00:41:17,533
<i>I doubt it.</i>

608
00:41:18,242 --> 00:41:19,409
<i>I mean nothing to them.</i>

609
00:41:21,662 --> 00:41:26,750
<i>BITTER SWEET</i>

610
00:41:29,628 --> 00:41:31,922
Oh, no. I guess I was right.

611
00:41:32,756 --> 00:41:34,883
<i>Did you really think
there was something going on?</i>

612
00:41:39,763 --> 00:41:41,056
<i>This is humiliating.</i>

613
00:41:42,349 --> 00:41:44,393
<i>Come to your senses, Nam Da-reum.</i>

614
00:41:45,269 --> 00:41:47,521
<i>You're just one of his numerous fans.</i>

615
00:42:16,300 --> 00:42:20,512
INCOMING CALL
CHAN

616
00:42:37,070 --> 00:42:38,655
Where on earth can I get it?

617
00:43:02,638 --> 00:43:03,639
Wait...

618
00:43:23,075 --> 00:43:24,076
Ms. Nam!

619
00:43:45,055 --> 00:43:46,056
Are you okay?

620
00:43:47,724 --> 00:43:48,725
Yes.

621
00:43:55,941 --> 00:43:57,317
Why aren't you watching
where you're going?

622
00:43:57,693 --> 00:43:59,736
Why did you cross the road
without checking the traffic light?

623
00:44:05,158 --> 00:44:06,243
I'm sorry.

624
00:44:09,287 --> 00:44:11,498
I couldn't see it.

625
00:44:14,209 --> 00:44:15,252
I really

626
00:44:16,461 --> 00:44:18,088
didn't see it.

627
00:44:23,093 --> 00:44:24,886
I know I was wrong.

628
00:44:26,763 --> 00:44:29,599
If you yell at me like that

629
00:44:33,437 --> 00:44:35,605
I don't know what to say.

630
00:44:52,414 --> 00:44:53,540
Sorry for getting mad at you.

631
00:44:54,875 --> 00:44:55,876
I was startled too.

632
00:44:58,378 --> 00:45:00,922
No, I'm sorry.

633
00:45:02,049 --> 00:45:03,091
Did

634
00:45:04,134 --> 00:45:05,135
something bad happen?

635
00:45:08,638 --> 00:45:09,681
No.

636
00:45:10,307 --> 00:45:13,018
Today was
the happiest day of my life.

637
00:45:18,690 --> 00:45:19,733
Something

638
00:45:21,068 --> 00:45:22,986
I'd always dreamed of
happened to me.

639
00:45:25,280 --> 00:45:26,323
But

640
00:45:27,741 --> 00:45:31,036
I didn't realize dreams end...

641
00:45:34,331 --> 00:45:35,332
once I wake up.

642
00:45:49,471 --> 00:45:50,472
Let's go.

643
00:45:51,014 --> 00:45:52,057
I'll take you home.

644
00:45:52,891 --> 00:45:53,892
Okay.

645
00:45:57,479 --> 00:45:58,480
Your bag.

646
00:45:58,980 --> 00:45:59,981
Oh, that's right.

647
00:46:05,529 --> 00:46:06,655
What's wrong with me?

648
00:46:17,040 --> 00:46:18,041
INKUK HOSPITAL

649
00:46:18,125 --> 00:46:19,167
<i>You sprained your ligament.</i>

650
00:46:19,835 --> 00:46:21,628
<i>You need to wear it
for at least two weeks.</i>

651
00:46:41,523 --> 00:46:43,817
I'm sorry. It's my fault.

652
00:46:48,655 --> 00:46:51,825
These are what I could find for now.
I thought you might need them.

653
00:46:53,952 --> 00:46:54,995
What are they?

654
00:47:08,216 --> 00:47:09,885
{\an8}RUBBER GLOVES

655
00:47:14,848 --> 00:47:15,932
What's this for?

656
00:47:28,653 --> 00:47:31,948
Shower with that on for tonight.
And tomorrow...

657
00:47:32,032 --> 00:47:33,116
Take this off now.

658
00:47:34,534 --> 00:47:35,577
Okay.

659
00:47:36,578 --> 00:47:37,913
I'll take it off.

660
00:47:58,225 --> 00:47:59,392
Oh, Mr. Kang.

661
00:48:01,144 --> 00:48:03,271
Mr. Kang, let me help you.

662
00:48:05,023 --> 00:48:06,024
Are you okay?

663
00:48:08,068 --> 00:48:11,029
Whenever I'm with you,
I have to watch my back and front.

664
00:48:11,112 --> 00:48:12,489
I just can't let my guard down.

665
00:48:14,074 --> 00:48:15,367
I'd better get going.

666
00:48:16,243 --> 00:48:18,620
I'm sorry, Mr. Kang.

667
00:48:20,580 --> 00:48:23,833
What am I going to do now?
I got into trouble again.

668
00:48:40,475 --> 00:48:41,518
Well...

669
00:48:41,935 --> 00:48:45,355
He just wanted to thank me
for being his fan for so long.

670
00:48:45,689 --> 00:48:49,109
We had dinner at his house.
That's all.

671
00:48:49,192 --> 00:48:50,944
Wait, you went to his house?

672
00:48:51,569 --> 00:48:53,446
How can you say
that's not a big deal?

673
00:48:53,655 --> 00:48:57,659
Normally, you would've made a scene
saying you couldn't believe it.

674
00:48:58,159 --> 00:48:59,286
But why are you so calm?

675
00:49:00,829 --> 00:49:02,872
- You're suspicious.
- You're suspicious.

676
00:49:06,084 --> 00:49:08,044
No, I'm not.

677
00:49:09,004 --> 00:49:11,673
I couldn't be happier.
I'm on cloud nine.

678
00:49:13,800 --> 00:49:17,887
When you experience
something completely unbelievable

679
00:49:18,388 --> 00:49:20,974
you become surprisingly calm.

680
00:49:24,936 --> 00:49:27,314
If that's the case,
I'm happy for you.

681
00:49:27,856 --> 00:49:29,190
I was worried for nothing.

682
00:49:34,863 --> 00:49:37,449
Did you see Namda's terrible acting?

683
00:49:40,160 --> 00:49:41,286
Something happened for sure.

684
00:49:41,953 --> 00:49:42,996
Something happened to her.

685
00:49:43,079 --> 00:49:44,998
She was excited to meet Chan.

686
00:49:45,999 --> 00:49:47,709
What the heck happened?

687
00:50:08,646 --> 00:50:10,648
I wonder if Mr. Kang is okay.

688
00:50:15,779 --> 00:50:18,865
He'd think I'm a total nuisance.

689
00:50:21,618 --> 00:50:24,996
He wouldn't use those red gloves.
What was I thinking?

690
00:50:25,080 --> 00:50:26,456
I'm such an idiot.

691
00:50:52,315 --> 00:50:55,026
So what happened to your arm?

692
00:50:55,110 --> 00:50:56,528
It was fine until the weekend.

693
00:50:56,611 --> 00:50:58,029
A dog came at me.

694
00:50:58,446 --> 00:51:01,324
How big was the dog
to leave your arm like that?

695
00:51:08,665 --> 00:51:09,666
Well, it was

696
00:51:11,209 --> 00:51:12,544
about the size of a Pomeranian.

697
00:51:12,627 --> 00:51:14,838
A Pomeranian?

698
00:51:15,713 --> 00:51:17,298
You mean a Pomeranian?

699
00:51:17,382 --> 00:51:18,383
Mr. Kang.

700
00:51:18,716 --> 00:51:19,968
We have a seat for you here.

701
00:51:21,177 --> 00:51:22,846
Come on. Join us.

702
00:51:27,016 --> 00:51:28,101
Have a seat.

703
00:51:31,688 --> 00:51:35,066
Excuse me. We'll get beef brisket
<i>doenjang </i>soup and <i>jeyuk</i>.

704
00:51:35,150 --> 00:51:36,192
Okay.

705
00:51:37,735 --> 00:51:39,070
Mr. Kang, your arm...

706
00:51:40,321 --> 00:51:42,490
Mr. Kang, what happened to your arm?

707
00:51:42,574 --> 00:51:43,783
Let me tell you what happened.

708
00:51:43,867 --> 00:51:46,202
A Pomeranian attacked his arm.

709
00:51:46,286 --> 00:51:48,580
- A Pomeranian?
- Yes, a Pomeranian.

710
00:51:48,663 --> 00:51:51,082
- The small dog?
- Yes, the small dog.

711
00:51:52,000 --> 00:51:54,002
- The cute one?
- Very cute.

712
00:51:54,085 --> 00:51:56,171
A lovely Pomeranian?

713
00:51:56,254 --> 00:51:58,047
The lovely Pomeranian.

714
00:52:02,969 --> 00:52:05,054
I fell.

715
00:52:05,930 --> 00:52:09,809
It must be uncomfortable, Mr. Kang.

716
00:52:10,852 --> 00:52:13,313
Still, you're lucky
it's your left arm

717
00:52:13,396 --> 00:52:14,772
not your right arm.

718
00:52:15,356 --> 00:52:16,524
I'm left-handed.

719
00:52:17,025 --> 00:52:19,444
Oh, I see.

720
00:52:20,487 --> 00:52:22,614
Let's eat.

721
00:52:22,697 --> 00:52:24,407
- Enjoy.
- Enjoy your meal.

722
00:52:29,662 --> 00:52:32,373
Oh, no. What do we do?

723
00:52:33,124 --> 00:52:34,584
- Here.
- Thank you.

724
00:52:34,667 --> 00:52:36,044
I'm worried.

725
00:52:40,673 --> 00:52:42,550
Mr. Kang.

726
00:52:42,717 --> 00:52:44,302
Do you want me to feed you?

727
00:52:46,679 --> 00:52:48,014
No, thank you.

728
00:52:48,097 --> 00:52:50,433
You're eating nothing but rice.

729
00:52:50,725 --> 00:52:51,726
I like rice.

730
00:52:51,809 --> 00:52:54,020
No, let me feed you. Here.

731
00:53:25,372 --> 00:53:30,920
<i>Mr. Kang, the overseas VC wants
to hear back from us by today.</i>

732
00:53:31,003 --> 00:53:32,421
<i>If you confirm it</i>

733
00:53:32,505 --> 00:53:34,548
I'll send the file now.
What do you think?

734
00:53:34,632 --> 00:53:36,050
<i>I want to fix a few pages.</i>

735
00:53:36,717 --> 00:53:37,801
Give me a few minutes.

736
00:53:38,344 --> 00:53:39,345
Bye.

737
00:53:58,364 --> 00:53:59,365
Shoot.

738
00:54:08,165 --> 00:54:09,208
APPELLO CEO KANG HA-GI

739
00:54:09,875 --> 00:54:14,463
<i>Mr. Kang, I'm sorry about all the...</i>

740
00:54:15,965 --> 00:54:17,258
No.

741
00:54:18,676 --> 00:54:19,760
What should I say?

742
00:54:23,264 --> 00:54:27,142
<i>Mr. Kang, if you need anything,
call me anytime...</i>

743
00:54:28,352 --> 00:54:29,937
No.

744
00:54:31,397 --> 00:54:33,732
Why do I keep causing Mr. Kang harm

745
00:54:33,816 --> 00:54:36,652
and nothing ever works out
when I'm with him?

746
00:54:38,320 --> 00:54:39,738
What should I say in the apology?

747
00:54:42,741 --> 00:54:45,953
Think. Think with your brain.

748
00:54:48,789 --> 00:54:49,790
CALLING APPELLO CEO KANG HA-GI

749
00:54:51,625 --> 00:54:52,626
INCOMING CALL
MS. NAM DA-REUM

750
00:55:01,677 --> 00:55:02,678
Hello?

751
00:55:04,555 --> 00:55:05,556
<i>Hello?</i>

752
00:55:06,265 --> 00:55:07,266
<i>Ms. Nam?</i>

753
00:55:08,601 --> 00:55:09,685
<i>Ms. Nam Da-reum?</i>

754
00:55:11,562 --> 00:55:13,772
Yes, Mr. Kang.

755
00:55:13,856 --> 00:55:15,190
<i>You must be off work by now.</i>

756
00:55:15,316 --> 00:55:17,610
Yes. What are you calling me for
at this hour?

757
00:55:18,944 --> 00:55:20,487
<i>Well, that's...</i>

758
00:55:23,407 --> 00:55:25,326
Your arm must be causing you
a lot of discomfort.

759
00:55:25,659 --> 00:55:28,078
I meant to text you
because I was concerned.

760
00:55:28,162 --> 00:55:30,331
But somehow I ended up calling you.

761
00:55:31,498 --> 00:55:33,834
<i>Yes, it's very uncomfortable.</i>

762
00:55:36,045 --> 00:55:37,254
Because of my arm

763
00:55:38,297 --> 00:55:40,090
I couldn't even fix
the urgent proposal.

764
00:55:41,800 --> 00:55:42,885
Really?

765
00:55:45,304 --> 00:55:47,181
That's not good.

766
00:55:47,264 --> 00:55:49,058
I'll go to your house now.

767
00:55:49,141 --> 00:55:51,268
<i>- We live in the same neighborhood.</i>
- What?

768
00:55:52,519 --> 00:55:53,562
But...

769
00:55:54,563 --> 00:55:56,482
You could just help me
at a cafe nearby...

770
00:55:56,565 --> 00:55:58,359
<i>No, you have an injured arm.</i>

771
00:55:58,442 --> 00:56:00,861
How would you bring your laptop
and materials with you?

772
00:56:01,945 --> 00:56:04,031
Just wait. I'll leave soon.

773
00:56:04,114 --> 00:56:05,240
<i>Ms. Nam Da-reum. Nam...</i>

774
00:56:05,532 --> 00:56:07,076
Ms. Nam... Ms. Nam?

775
00:56:18,337 --> 00:56:19,463
Shoot.

776
00:56:38,065 --> 00:56:41,110
<i>This is my chance to make up
for being a nuisance.</i>

777
00:56:41,527 --> 00:56:43,612
<i>Mr. Kang, just wait.</i>

778
00:56:43,696 --> 00:56:45,989
<i>My 600-character-per-minute fingers
are coming.</i>

779
00:56:50,369 --> 00:56:52,913
This is Ha-gi's favorite wine.

780
00:57:03,090 --> 00:57:04,341
I'm here.

781
00:57:08,846 --> 00:57:11,265
Mr. Kang, I'm here.

782
00:57:12,641 --> 00:57:13,642
Okay.

783
00:57:21,567 --> 00:57:24,570
- Hello.
- Ms. Nam.

784
00:57:24,987 --> 00:57:26,697
- That was fast.
- Yes.

785
00:57:27,197 --> 00:57:29,283
Your house is so close.

786
00:57:29,366 --> 00:57:31,285
It's only 500m away from my house.

787
00:57:32,870 --> 00:57:34,621
- Did you run here?
- Yes.

788
00:57:34,872 --> 00:57:36,248
You need to send the proposal soon.

789
00:57:52,097 --> 00:57:53,724
Oh, thank you.

790
00:57:58,479 --> 00:58:00,272
- Where do you want me to work on it?
- What?

791
00:58:02,232 --> 00:58:04,818
Here. No, there.

792
00:58:04,902 --> 00:58:07,196
Oh, how about next to your laptop?

793
00:58:32,805 --> 00:58:35,557
- Mr. Kang, are you okay?
- Yes, I'm okay.

794
00:58:40,020 --> 00:58:41,480
- Mr. Kang.
- Yes?

795
00:58:42,105 --> 00:58:43,148
Is this the one?

796
00:58:44,650 --> 00:58:46,235
Oh, yes.

797
00:58:46,568 --> 00:58:47,569
Then...

798
00:58:49,822 --> 00:58:52,032
It's inconvenient
to look at the monitors this way.

799
00:58:53,158 --> 00:58:54,451
I'll move next to you.

800
00:59:06,964 --> 00:59:08,507
What do you need to add?

801
00:59:12,553 --> 00:59:14,054
- Mr. Kang?
- Yes?

802
00:59:15,013 --> 00:59:16,181
Did you hear what I said?

803
00:59:17,057 --> 00:59:18,267
You need to tell me what to add.

804
00:59:19,726 --> 00:59:21,019
Oh, yes. Right.

805
00:59:22,771 --> 00:59:25,148
- How did I miss that?
- Focus.

806
00:59:26,275 --> 00:59:27,276
Okay.

807
00:59:28,193 --> 00:59:29,194
Focus.

808
00:59:30,404 --> 00:59:32,865
I wanted to add some data
to the original pitch deck.

809
00:59:32,948 --> 00:59:36,076
The CEO of this VC considers
CSR important.

810
00:59:37,452 --> 00:59:40,080
Are you trying to emphasize

811
00:59:40,163 --> 00:59:41,623
Appello's mission of mutual growth?

812
00:59:42,499 --> 00:59:44,251
Yes, that's correct.

813
00:59:44,459 --> 00:59:48,046
Then, how about using the last
online fashion show as an example?

814
00:59:50,382 --> 00:59:52,593
It has a visual impact

815
00:59:52,676 --> 00:59:55,971
and emphasizes
that we're a fashion company.

816
00:59:56,430 --> 00:59:57,514
That's a good idea.

817
00:59:57,764 --> 00:59:59,641
Yes, I'll go with that then.

818
01:00:15,157 --> 01:00:16,867
Delete this.

819
01:00:17,451 --> 01:00:19,620
- Say that it was done in real time.
- Okay.

820
01:00:21,163 --> 01:00:22,372
Add real time...

821
01:00:24,124 --> 01:00:25,375
Again...

822
01:00:30,505 --> 01:00:32,549
THIS IS THE FINAL VERSION

823
01:00:33,050 --> 01:00:34,051
SEND

824
01:00:34,551 --> 01:00:35,636
SUCCESSFULLY SENT

825
01:00:35,719 --> 01:00:37,012
It's sent.

826
01:00:47,481 --> 01:00:48,482
What?

827
01:00:59,534 --> 01:01:00,953
What a relief.

828
01:01:11,838 --> 01:01:14,800
I've sent the edited version.
Can you check it?

829
01:01:38,407 --> 01:01:40,325
I was able to handle
the urgent matter thanks to you.

830
01:01:40,909 --> 01:01:42,369
- Thank you.
- Don't mention it.

831
01:01:42,786 --> 01:01:44,871
You're in that state because of me.

832
01:01:45,247 --> 01:01:46,331
This is the least I could do.

833
01:01:47,332 --> 01:01:49,334
By the way, Mr. Kang.

834
01:01:51,086 --> 01:01:53,547
